{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game","id":1152201,"title":"The ideal WoD video game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-23T07:59:49-07:00","id":1152201,"title":"The ideal WoD video game","content":"So...<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about how to create a good WoD game: it's not easy. As has been discussed on the forum before many of the disciplines are not what might be called &quot;game friendly&quot;, most are designed for situations that might arise during a specific moment in the story. Say you had a game like, for example, Skyrim: You have enough dots invested in necromancy to summon a spirit just to ask one question? How do you simulate that? what would happen if you used that discipline when wondering about the game world? It really wouldn't be something a player could just use whenever.<br /> <br /> That's why I think the best way to go about making a WoD video game is to create a Telltale/David Kage style interactive game. This would create a game with the cinematic quality of many other titles, but with the ability for the developers to bring in any and all mechanics from the original sourcebooks, because those mechanics would only come into play when needed.<br /> <br /> Let's see if I can't give an example:<br /> <br /> Say you have a dialog scene, if you have the &quot;dominate&quot; discipline, and depending on how high you have leveled it, you get dialog options you wouldn't otherwise.<br /> <br /> Or a scene begins where your character enters some social gathering and, if he/she has invested into the Presence discipline, they get a prompt at the opening of the scene with something like &quot;Awe&quot; and instantly the people in the room react differently than they would if playing a character without any dots invested in presence.<br /> <br /> Or if you have a QTE-driven fight-scene, you have options to drop-kick or throw a sink at your opponent, or, if you have enough dots invested in potence, you also get an option to rip a phone-booth off the ground and toss it at them.<br /> <br /> Everything would be contextual, and only come into play when the story demands it.<br /> <br /> You could also make it episodic, like a Telltale game, with different &quot;seasons&quot; focusing on different parts of the WoD: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Carimilla, season in which you can choose from and play as one of the Caramilla clans.</li> <li>Anarchy: story-line focused on the anarchs.</li> <li>Sabbat: season focused on the Sabbat where you choose to play either Tzimisce or Lasombra.</li> <li>Hunters Hunted: season focused on hunters, where player chooses to play as a hunter from the Government, Society of Leopold, the Arcaneum, or just an average vampire-hunting Joe.</li> </ol><br /> And you could have many more, all to be played separately, but released as updates for the same game.<br /> <br /> Last, but by no means least: players should be given a comprehensive suite of mod tools, like the ones given for Bethesda games, allowing players to use the games engine and assets to construct their own &quot;seasons&quot; or just stand-alone &quot;movies&quot; and share them with others.<br /> <br /> It would, IMO be the best way to bring the WoD experience to video game format.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T11:31:45-07:00","id":1152243,"title":"","content":"My ideal WoD game is Bloodlines with around 6 more months of development time.<br /> <br /> As it stands, it's still pretty damn amazing(as is Redemption). <br /> <br /> But you do have some good ideas...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-23T12:11:36-07:00","id":1152253,"title":"","content":"An idea? An indie game playable on Android<br /> <br /> playing as either a garou or Kithain, managing a sept or freehold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T13:32:04-07:00","id":1152906,"title":"","content":"I would enjoy seeing something that combined the open world sandbox style thats become so big in the past decade done as very large city with a wide diversity of neighborhoods and some surrounding suburban and rural areas, with the level or roleplaying and &quot;your actions impact the setting&quot; even bigger than some of the more recent roleplaying games, and an extreme amount of character customization, not just with power/ability paths, but also with what your character wears, uses as weapons or even drives. And as part of all that, being able to take over buildings/neighborhoods and remake/renovate them to whatever fits your needs and goals. If, for example, my vampire character gains control over a small club, I want to be able to grow and customize said club into a major power base, and have it look and feel the way I want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T16:09:49-07:00","id":1152968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1152906#post1152906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would enjoy seeing something that combined the open world sandbox style thats become so big in the past decade done as very large city with a wide diversity of neighborhoods and some surrounding suburban and rural areas, with the level or roleplaying and &quot;your actions impact the setting&quot; even bigger than some of the more recent roleplaying games, and an extreme amount of character customization, not just with power/ability paths, but also with what your character wears, uses as weapons or even drives. And as part of all that, being able to take over buildings/neighborhoods and remake/renovate them to whatever fits your needs and goals. If, for example, my vampire character gains control over a small club, I want to be able to grow and customize said club into a major power base, and have it look and feel the way I want.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be interesting, but again you run into the problem of accurately simulating certain disciplines in an open-world game like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T18:20:25-07:00","id":1152996,"title":"","content":"what about umbral realms? wouldnt it be fun to be able to explore some of them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T05:59:12-07:00","id":1153720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1152996#post1152996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what about umbral realms? wouldnt it be fun to be able to explore some of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, just like a Telltale-style game, it would be a contextual thing, some scenes take place in the Umbra, others would allow you the choice to travel there, all as the story demands or allows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11522-the_1990","name":"the_1990","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T11:17:24-07:00","id":1155797,"title":"","content":"Your idea is good, but it is also Bloodlines, already. Well, most of it. So yes, that would certainly be the ideal WoD game.<br /> <br /> We just need a producer company that won't go bankruptcy before finishing it and to pay WW for the rights.<br /> <br /> Paying for the rights is, actually, the easy part. They actively tried this several times before, and are trying it again. To find a company that can actually survive until delivery is the tricky proposition.<br /> <br /> I like the mod creator idea, pretty much, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T11:47:58-08:00","id":1157325,"title":"","content":"I don't think that there's a way to create ideal WoD video game. There's too much genres of video games. But I've got some ideas, sometimes inspired by events from my games or official books:<br /> <br /> Jungle War - a strategy game resembling Star Wars Rebellion. The story: Golgol Fangs First is dead. You are his succesor. You have to win the Amazon War. You have to send the packs to fight, send recruiters to the other septs to gain support for your efforts. And also battles could be implemented into the game, either RTS style, like in Total War series or tactical, like in Jagged Alliance.<br /> Red Carpet Fighting Club - inspired by Giovanni Chronicles part IV. A fighting game. Choose a fighter or create your own (standard today) and win the illegal tournament organized by Giovanni clan mobsters. Optional there could be bribery to ease the game or betting (like in The Con video game). And roaring 20's jazz in the background. <br /> EWW - wrestling video game inspired by Children of the Night book. Choose or create a wrestler (mortal or supernatural) and become the champion in Pentex owned wrestling federation. Also it could include managerial options. <br /> Corporate Wolf - inspired by events from my games. Business simulation game. The plot: finally Glass Walkers convinced other tribes that to defeat the Wyrm is to tackle Pentex. You are Michael Donelly, a Glass Walker Philodox investor to which entire garou nation money was given. Your goal: eliminate every Pentex company one by one. Choose your path by dominating the global market.<br /> Prince of the City - inspired by Sim City and The Sims. Simulation of a Camarilla Prince. I've read once about Simsville, a game never released but resembling this concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-09-2017, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T15:57:06-08:00","id":1157380,"title":"","content":"Changeling Kings:A game of fairy politics and war in the back drop of the modern world. Using C:TD Lore to build something akin to Crusader Kings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T17:04:26-08:00","id":1157398,"title":"","content":"Another idea: The Rack - a nightclub management game. You are the owner of nightclub which is an Elysium and you have to take care for it. This means maintaining the supply, the Masquerade and sometimes Lupines attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T21:19:38-08:00","id":1157448,"title":"","content":"I think there's a lot of potential in a First Person Shooter/Horror game, where you play a Progenitor in a Damage Control cleanup squad. Your job is to descend into the worst places imaginable, and clean out the biological horror that tends to populate the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Etherite labs full of Frankenstein monsters. Giovanni mansions riddled with zombies. A Tzimisce's haven; 'nuff said. A Wyrm-tainted swamp full of inbred cannibal Fomori, and their &quot;pets&quot;. A Black Spiral Dancer Caern. A wraith-haunted house full of Risen. A Chinese office building that is haven to some out-of-control Devil Tigers. A Shallowing that has allowed grotesque or strange Umbral entities wreak havoc in material form. A Nosferatu sewer warren, complete with breeding pools and ghouled animals. A secret, underground infernalist temple full of demons. A Nephandi labyrinth, complete with a battle where the player has to fight off monsters and transformed Fallen mages that try to force the player into a Caul. A Baali pit, where the player must descend through a mountain of corpses to reach the bottom. A fight in a former Technocracy Construct out in the Umbra, currently under the management of Threat Null. A descent into an underwater Technocracy base, which has been overrun by deep sea Cthuloid horrors.<br /> <br /> And then, the last mission, having to fight their way into a Union stronghold, currently overrun by rampaging Technocratic biological experiments. At the end, you might find out that the one responsible is a Nephandi infiltrator, and you have to purge the Union of their taint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-09T22:08:47-08:00","id":1157459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157448#post1157448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a lot of potential in a First Person Shooter/Horror game, where you play a Progenitor in a Damage Control cleanup squad. Your job is to descend into the worst places imaginable, and clean out the biological horror that tends to populate the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Etherite labs full of Frankenstein monsters. Giovanni mansions riddled with zombies. A Tzimisce's haven; 'nuff said. A Wyrm-tainted swamp full of inbred cannibal Fomori, and their &quot;pets&quot;. A Black Spiral Dancer Caern. A wraith-haunted house full of Risen. A Chinese office building that is haven to some out-of-control Devil Tigers. A Shallowing that has allowed grotesque or strange Umbral entities wreak havoc in material form. A Nosferatu sewer warren, complete with breeding pools and ghouled animals. A secret, underground infernalist temple full of demons. A Nephandi labyrinth, complete with a battle where the player has to fight off monsters and transformed Fallen mages that try to force the player into a Caul. A Baali pit, where the player must descend through a mountain of corpses to reach the bottom. A fight in a former Technocracy Construct out in the Umbra, currently under the management of Threat Null. A descent into an underwater Technocracy base, which has been overrun by deep sea Cthuloid horrors.<br /> <br /> And then, the last mission, having to fight their way into a Union stronghold, currently overrun by rampaging Technocratic biological experiments. At the end, you might find out that the one responsible is a Nephandi infiltrator, and you have to purge the Union of their taint.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd play the fuck out of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T05:50:33-08:00","id":1157506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157448#post1157448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a lot of potential in a First Person Shooter/Horror game, where you play a Progenitor in a Damage Control cleanup squad. Your job is to descend into the worst places imaginable, and clean out the biological horror that tends to populate the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Etherite labs full of Frankenstein monsters. Giovanni mansions riddled with zombies. A Tzimisce's haven; 'nuff said. A Wyrm-tainted swamp full of inbred cannibal Fomori, and their &quot;pets&quot;. A Black Spiral Dancer Caern. A wraith-haunted house full of Risen. A Chinese office building that is haven to some out-of-control Devil Tigers. A Shallowing that has allowed grotesque or strange Umbral entities wreak havoc in material form. A Nosferatu sewer warren, complete with breeding pools and ghouled animals. A secret, underground infernalist temple full of demons. A Nephandi labyrinth, complete with a battle where the player has to fight off monsters and transformed Fallen mages that try to force the player into a Caul. A Baali pit, where the player must descend through a mountain of corpses to reach the bottom. A fight in a former Technocracy Construct out in the Umbra, currently under the management of Threat Null. A descent into an underwater Technocracy base, which has been overrun by deep sea Cthuloid horrors.<br /> <br /> And then, the last mission, having to fight their way into a Union stronghold, currently overrun by rampaging Technocratic biological experiments. At the end, you might find out that the one responsible is a Nephandi infiltrator, and you have to purge the Union of their taint.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's how Doom was created :P. But seriously don't we have enough shooters in WoD video games? Redemption was a spoiled idea; hack&amp;slash/shooter, Hunter: the Reckoning games were shooters, both Werewolf concepts were shooters even so highly praised Bloodlines had many missions like &quot;kill anything in sight, sell their equipement, go to the next level &quot;. This time the only difference would be point of view. In my opinion a film noir point'n'klick adventure (like Blade Runner) would be better. Shooter/survival horror should be additions. Secondly remember that if Damage Control would be so straightforward insted of their common subtletly there would be no Masquerade or Veil, they would be broker. And then you will have your survival horror: &quot;(...)Now they know. Nobody knows where they've found this knowledge but they know. About you, about your race, even about your enemies. Play as a shapeshifter, vampire, mage, wraith or changeling and defend yourself against angry human mob. See what it means to be hunted(...)&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T14:31:12-08:00","id":1157638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157506#post1157506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But seriously don't we have enough shooters in WoD video games? Redemption was a spoiled idea; hack&amp;slash/shooter, Hunter: the Reckoning games were shooters, both Werewolf concepts were shooters.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are really, REALLY wrong.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T21:54:03-08:00","id":1157696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157638#post1157638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You are really, REALLY wrong.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T06:03:19-08:00","id":1157734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157696#post1157696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why do you think so?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because the poster you quoted said First Person Shooters. None of those games you mentioned are first person shooters. <br /> <br /> Even if you want to go with &quot;shooters,&quot; instead...Redemption was in no way a shooter, Hunter the Reckoning is not a shooter. Bloodlines is a shooter, the same way that Tetris is an action-rpg. Neither of the two cancelled Werewolf games are shooters.<br /> <br /> This forum is also not a shooter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T07:39:31-08:00","id":1157747,"title":"","content":"As much as I'm not a fan of FPS myself, I have nothing wrong with the genre, and definitely we didn't had any true FPS as a WoD game.<br /> <br /> Every kind of game can be used to great effect to show facets of the WoD. Mostly my doubt would be about the mechanics to implement the interesting mechanics of each line in a video game. But I can see a Mage-based shooter working with an R&amp;D platform for devising weapons, armor, itens and other options. Instead of getting ammo and items through stages, you get materials and new routes, and devise your own stuff with it.<br /> <br /> You could have some resources admin games also. A game where you're an Elder vampire/werewolf/mage running your piece of the whole. One of those could be simple enough to be an app.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T16:44:41-08:00","id":1157832,"title":"","content":"OK. But I was thinking about shooters generally, not only FPS. If you want me to be precise: Hunters were action games, Redemption was an action game with a drop of RPG, first Werewolf (the one for Sega) was an action game, Heart of Gaia was supposed to be an action game with a drop of RPG. Bloodlines was the closest one to RPG. Role playing games is something more than just getting xps and raising your stats. Harley Davidson Road to Sturgis wasn't a RPG game either, even if you create a character and raise your characteristics during the game. But I must admit that I don't like most but a few FPS. Maybe it's because I have a storyteller's quirk and I think that there's more heroes in this world than just one. And in most FPS games there's only one hero: the PC. So when I hear (and in this case read) about FPS game based on Damage Control I see this: DC has only one effective agent. If somebody (player characters p. ex.) kill him the Technocracy will be doomed. And that looks silly to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T16:54:53-08:00","id":1157834,"title":"","content":"As for WoD video games ideas: a caern builder. You found an abandoned/destroyed caern and you have to to make it functional again. You have to choose the participants of the rite from incoming characters (like in HOM&amp;M) basing on their auspice and tribe to avoid conflicts (like in Jagged Alliance or Baldurs Gate), choose the best moment for a rite (so the caern could be effectively reopened; and there should be enough garou to perform the rite), defend it (RTT or turn based tactical game elements) and organise the sept to avoid conflicts (Sims like elements).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T19:10:49-08:00","id":1157852,"title":"","content":"Well, that is a bit tad true. Though action games are fun, they are not the only genre around, but were the most focused until now.<br /> <br /> Either way, still valid as an idea. But we still need someone that can actually pull this off. How much is White-Wolf asking for the license, someone knows?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T20:40:34-08:00","id":1157865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157852#post1157852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Either way, still valid as an idea. But we still need someone that can actually pull this off. How much is White-Wolf asking for the license, someone knows?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I see it, judging by my experience as a rock band manager it's all about demand. Let's be honest, most popular RPGs are D&amp;D and Warhammer. And they will exist in our computers/consoles always. The second thing is the price of a licence. I think that's the reason of Mechwarrior and Battletech video games availability. As far as I know WW is rather territorial about their universe so I suppose that the price could be high. But if we could prove to the biggest in the video gaming world that we would love to spend money for their games if they would set them in the WoD maybe we will convince them to invest their money into creating game like that.<br /> <br /> Also Kickstarter could be useful. My strategy: 2 steps. If the first one would be reached the subscribers will get a generic werewolf/vampire/mage/etc game. But if the next level would be reached then there will be money for a licence and the game could be upgraded to a real WoD game. Of course we have to find the squad which could do that.<br /> <br /> Third option is something between the first two. We could create a game (the story, concept arts etc) and send them to some developer asking if they will be interested. I know it's rather insolent move but a good negotiator could convince them to join forces. They could save money on creators and artists. And my personal motto for situations like that? If we don't try we won't succeed. But if we try there's a slight chance that we will. Remember George Lucas: he tried to sell Star Wars to 4 studios but the fifth was 20th Century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-12-2017, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-11T21:19:41-08:00","id":1157868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157865#post1157865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I see it, judging by my experience as a rock band manager it's all about demand. Let's be honest, most popular RPGs are D&amp;D and Warhammer. And they will exist in our computers/consoles always. The second thing is the price of a licence. I think that's the reason of Mechwarrior and Battletech video games availability. As far as I know WW is rather territorial about their universe so I suppose that the price could be high. But if we could prove to the biggest in the video gaming world that we would love to spend money for their games if they would set them in the WoD maybe we will convince them to invest their money into creating game like that.<br /> <br /> Also Kickstarter could be useful. My strategy: 2 steps. If the first one would be reached the subscribers will get a generic werewolf/vampire/mage/etc game. But if the next level would be reached then there will be money for a licence and the game could be upgraded to a real WoD game. Of course we have to find the squad which could do that.<br /> <br /> Third option is something between the first two. We could create a game (the story, concept arts etc) and send them to some developer asking if they will be interested. I know it's rather insolent move but a good negotiator could convince them to join forces. They could save money on creators and artists. And my personal motto for situations like that? If we don't try we won't succeed. But if we try there's a slight chance that we will. Remember George Lucas: he tried to sell Star Wars to 4 studios but the fifth was 20th Century.</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite territoriality, White Wolf tried to make WoD into the video-game market several times, already. And their new focus is on selling the license, so I'm not sure if it would be so expensive.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm on board on the last two options. Well established companies are unlikely to invest on this for now, and that isn't something I can help to achieve. But I can help with more hands-on projects, at least on the game concepts, story and some management. What we need first is workforce.<br /> <br /> Once we have this workforce, then we will know what we can achieve, and choose between the two options. As an ideal plan, if we can get enough hands we can Kickstart the project. It will be a long way through development, but we can have a saying on the final product and a share of any actual money we can get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T00:28:36-08:00","id":1157893,"title":"","content":"The reason I suggested a shooter was because it would be the most likely model to appeal to current video game trends. Damage Control as a faction within the Progenitors provides a good way to pit the player against a varied cross-section of the World of Darkness. And if the player character was a person who went into combat regularly, their Enlightened Science would trend more towards the sorts of mechanics that could be implemented in a modern shooter.<br /> <br /> The game could include a progression tree, where they would receive XP that could be used to unlock greater Sphere abilities, and therefore different tech. If the player wanted bullet time, they'd invest in Time. If they wanted to gain a self-heal, they'd invest into Life. Etc, etc. And the abilities themselves could involve tinkering with gadgets (or Gadgets), undergoing gene therapy, injecting super drugs, getting cybernetic implants from Iteration X, learning special martial arts moves, etc. No video game would be able to give players the unlimited options afforded in the base Mage game, but it would give the player all the options that would make sense given the PC's Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T05:35:46-08:00","id":1157911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157868#post1157868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite territoriality, White Wolf tried to make WoD into the video-game market several times, already. And their new focus is on selling the license, so I'm not sure if it would be so expensive.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm on board on the last two options. Well established companies are unlikely to invest on this for now, and that isn't something I can help to achieve. But I can help with more hands-on projects, at least on the game concepts, story and some management. What we need first is workforce.<br /> <br /> Once we have this workforce, then we will know what we can achieve, and choose between the two options. As an ideal plan, if we can get enough hands we can Kickstart the project. It will be a long way through development, but we can have a saying on the final product and a share of any actual money we can get.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've once read about a guy who tried to rebuild Heart of Gaia from scraps. And WW told him to stop. So I think they're rather sensitive about their licence. The games they've published were created by rather big companies which could afford the lincence fees. But I hope that merging with Paradox could change that.<br /> <br /> As for me I could be useful as a negotiator, I could create NPCs and stories and If we find some musicians I could also give some of my lyrics to make music for the game. They are inspired by W:tA mostly, with an idea to be NWOBHM style, mostly pro ecological (no lifting the Veil please). To give you some examples the titles are &quot;Living Concrete&quot;, &quot;The right to live&quot; or &quot;Glass Walking&quot;.<br /> <br /> I also hope that they will try to reactivate WoD MMO. I don't like most FPS games, most action games or RTS. But I was also thinking about a perfect game for me, which could be used to as a help for STs. And I ended with an idea of a game resembling The Sims, for adults of course, for supernaturals (something like The Sims Nightlife). And the quests could be published as mods or DLCs. Of course it would also have multiplayer option, even if I don't like MMO because I saw too many people playing those games and not feeling the climate of those games. There could also be the possibility to export your characters to other WoD games (maybe using my other ideas) so you could be anyone (a businessman in Corporate Wolf, the commander in Jungle War; see my previous posts). Imagine a game which, with all additions, could give you a chance to play without ST <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-12-2017, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T06:28:00-08:00","id":1157918,"title":"","content":"What we do need now is a place to organize things, starting by whatever staff we can get, with personal abilities and preferences.<br /> <br /> I do not see the need for defining the project right now, since we need to now what we will be actually able to do. Also, it is important to have commitment to the project as a whole, since it is quite unlikely that we will have unanimity on anything, so anyone wanting to participate will have to make compromises in a regular basis.<br /> <br /> Once this start, and depending on what we have to work with, we can get &quot;ambitious&quot; and try more than one model of game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T06:35:50-08:00","id":1157919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157893#post1157893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason I suggested a shooter was because it would be the most likely model to appeal to current video game trends. Damage Control as a faction within the Progenitors provides a good way to pit the player against a varied cross-section of the World of Darkness. And if the player character was a person who went into combat regularly, their Enlightened Science would trend more towards the sorts of mechanics that could be implemented in a modern shooter.<br /> <br /> The game could include a progression tree, where they would receive XP that could be used to unlock greater Sphere abilities, and therefore different tech. If the player wanted bullet time, they'd invest in Time. If they wanted to gain a self-heal, they'd invest into Life. Etc, etc. And the abilities themselves could involve tinkering with gadgets (or Gadgets), undergoing gene therapy, injecting super drugs, getting cybernetic implants from Iteration X, learning special martial arts moves, etc. No video game would be able to give players the unlimited options afforded in the base Mage game, but it would give the player all the options that would make sense given the PC's Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OK, I can see what you're thinking about. I can admit that the idea isn't bad but still I don't like most FPS<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I would rather see that game SWAT like or Rainbow Six like (because as far as I know DC rather work as teams). You know, first of all you have to create a plan, give orders and react if something goes wrong. And, as I like to go through the games without save&amp;load method I would modify your idea: you can upgrade your character the way you want it. Advancement of the rest of the team is controled by AI. If you lose one of your soldiers you will get a new one, a greenhorn. And if your character is killed you can load your game or proceed choosing one of your team (for hard core players like me). Or the FPS could be only an element. First you have to find the target (an RPG/adventure part of the game) then attack (FPS/tactical part). That would look like in Mechwarrior or Warhammer tabletop games, first the roleplay part than the battle. Or, as you advance you could act as a commander, you get the intel, choose the team and let the AI do the rest or choose to lead the attack (if I remember well Wings over Vietnam has gameplay like that).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T06:41:14-08:00","id":1157920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157918#post1157918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What we do need now is a place to organize things, starting by whatever staff we can get, with personal abilities and preferences.<br /> <br /> I do not see the need for defining the project right now, since we need to now what we will be actually able to do. Also, it is important to have commitment to the project as a whole, since it is quite unlikely that we will have unanimity on anything, so anyone wanting to participate will have to make compromises in a regular basis.<br /> <br /> Once this start, and depending on what we have to work with, we can get &quot;ambitious&quot; and try more than one model of game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, my other quirk is that I'm some kind of a visionary, I like to plan events in my games for many years to come not thinking if my PCs will survive their next adventure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> As for place I think that many of us will have trouble meeting each other so we have to organize this here, on this forum and find someone who will put our ideas into the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-12-2017, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T10:49:59-08:00","id":1157961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157920#post1157920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry, my other quirk is that I'm some kind of a visionary, I like to plan events in my games for many years to come not thinking if my PCs will survive their next adventure <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> As for place I think that many of us will have trouble meeting each other so we have to organize this here, on this forum and find someone who will put our ideas into the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem with breeding ideas, I'll assume the role of keeping us grounded for now, justa wanted to remember that things can go wildly different from our personal expectations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame\"> Development Board: Classic WoD Videogame - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So, we are going to try and create our own WoD videogame. This isn't going to be quick or easy, but if enough people want it done, it will be done. To this end, </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T17:51:58-08:00","id":1158039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1157961#post1157961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No problem with breeding ideas, I'll assume the role of keeping us grounded for now, justa wanted to remember that things can go wildly different from our personal expectations.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1157960-development-board-classic-wod-videogame\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-wod-videogame</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I know. Best laid plan etc. But I'm still excited 'bout this project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-13T04:02:43-08:00","id":1158125,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see something like a Grand Theft Auto type sandbox game based on Vampire, but without the metaplot. Something based on First Edition, and maybe even using the NPC's and setting from Chicago by Night.<br /> <br /> You could even make it a 1990's period piece to satisfy both the metaplot purists and people like me who don't like the metaplot, but love the early material for Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T03:38:50-08:00","id":1158405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1158125#post1158125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see something like a Grand Theft Auto type sandbox game based on Vampire, but without the metaplot. Something based on First Edition, and maybe even using the NPC's and setting from Chicago by Night.<br /> <br /> You could even make it a 1990's period piece to satisfy both the metaplot purists and people like me who don't like the metaplot, but love the early material for Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I have to admit that the setting in CbN is the closest to ideal. If I remember well the ST can build almost entire city population of supernaturals basing on various books: vampires were described in Chicago by Night, werewolves in Under a Blood Red Moon, small base of hunter's operations (Inquisition, not Hunters) in Inquisition sourcebook and Hollow Ones chantry but I don't remember where. This leaves only wraith and faeries to describe.<br /> <br /> As for metaplot I also don't like many of its elements but I still use it sometimes. To my campaigns (I don't like short stories) I put some turning points. If PC (or sometimes NPCs, sometimes it's better to use someone else) resolve them well (one by one, not all at one time) they push the Gehenna/Apocalypse further away. But if they fail the end of the world is nearer and some bad things happen: first the Week of Nightmares then one of Apocalypse/Gehenna scenario, including my own version of them. Some are almost invisible to the world (like the first one from Time of Judgement Apocalypse book) and if the last battle is won by &quot;the good guys&quot; the world lives on, while some brings the end in one big badaboom. So maybe you would like to play a game in which you can make Week of Nightmares happen or not. Just like in Transylvania Chronicles the PCs can shape the Camarilla or the Sabbath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-14-2017, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-09T23:47:38-08:00","id":1174793,"title":"","content":"I actually think that Changeling, the Dreaming could work from a Call of Cthulhu narrative in which your character swings in and out of 'reality' during the course of the story. And because of the Mists, you (or at least your character) is never quite sure what is real and what isn't. So, when a dragon suddenly falls out of the sky and starts wrecking shit in the chimerical reality, your character has to fight it off, but everybody around you is convinced you're having a psychotic fit. This gradually takes its toll as the story progresses, until you're in danger of being thrown into a padded cell, thus emphasizing the personal horror that Changelings have to go through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T21:03:29-08:00","id":1176455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1152201-the-ideal-wod-video-game?p=1174793#post1174793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think that Changeling, the Dreaming could work from a Call of Cthulhu narrative in which your character swings in and out of 'reality' during the course of the story. And because of the Mists, you (or at least your character) is never quite sure what is real and what isn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't Cthulhu-based but I've heard of a Japanese game that was something like that. It had an anime based on it. The name of the anime was something like &quot;Chaos;Head&quot; and you play someone who is at least partially delusional. As I understand it, gameplay allowed you to select different layers of reality to tackle a challenge with, and each choice had benefits and hindrances. So in effect not far off from Changeling or maybe specifically playing an Enchanted-style kinain.<br /> <br /> A more kinain-centric variant on the same style of game might go something like, sure you can take a hit from Grandma Maybell's hand-made Best Peanut Butter Cookies Ever, but you'll be dodging beasties and overly-friendly rainbows that follow you around like lost puppies for the next few hours. That might be okay if you're mobile but if you have to take the bus or think you might get hauled off to the police station sometime soon, it might be a very, very bad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23656-lanir","name":"Lanir","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-20T18:00:43-08:00","id":1177736,"title":"","content":"Something like X-COM would be quite affordable in doing Garou/Pentex/Technocracy/Midnight seige games. <br /> <br /> Other than that? bloodlines could've been better in half a hundred ways. Something more dynamic/open worlded/closer to the source would be great but monumentally expensive (command might work with voice control, but mesmerise would be damn near impossible). I think the core disciplines of the seven main clans, and some of the others, would be doable for player characters in a more book-accurate form if money/time wasn't such an issue.<br /> <br /> CRPGs would fit great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Be correct.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23728-pewpew","name":"PewPew","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}